{
  "notes": "Ambient, F minor (aeolian), 60 BPM. A drawbar organ on its slow rotary speaker (the orbit you hear turning), a felt piano that circles a seven-eighth figure (F C Eb G Eb C, rest) so it drifts against the bar and comes back into line only every seven bars, the player's looped strings on the Smart Keys (minor pentatonic from F3), and a soft sampled kit. The orbit figure uses only F G Bb C Eb, which sit well over every chord here (i9, VImaj7, iv9, VII, III), so it needs no chord tokens and can be any length. Scenes: A two chords of four bars; B an eccentric cycle, i9 and VImaj7 for three bars each and iv9 for two; C closer and brighter, VI VII III i two bars each with a five-eighth orbit; D the far point: VImaj7 held for eight bars, the orbit thinned to two notes. All material is original.",
